{
  "title": "Namaz of the Hungry",
  "data": "One who feels hungry may perform the ritual ablution (wudu), offer a two-unit prayer, and then say:\nيَا رَبِّ اِنِّيْ جَآئِعٌ فَاَطْعِمْنِيْ\nYAA RABBI INNEE JAA'I'UN FA-AT'IMNEE\nO my Lord, I am hungry, so feed me.\nAccording to another tradition, the supplication is as follows:\nرَبِّ اَطْعِمْنِيْ فَاِنِّيْ جَآئِعٌ\nRABBI AT'IMNEE FA-INNEE JAA'I'\nMy Lord, feed me, for I am hungry.",
  "merits": "Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said this. If one does so, Almighty Allah will immediately give him food."
}
